  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Sichuan opera (chuanju) Chinese regional opera tradition of the Sichuan basin (Chengdu, Chongqing, and broader province), synthesizing five distinct musical styles: gaoqiang (high-pitched), kunqiang (kunqu-derived), huqin (string-led), tanxi (clapper-style), and dengdiao (Sichuan-folk-derived) into a single eclectic theatrical tradition. The chuanju is particularly known for the \"face-changing\" (bian lian) stagecraft technique where the performer switches painted masks in fractions of a second through hidden mechanisms. Performance integrates voice, stylized dance-movement, recited dialogue, percussion-led ensemble, and elaborate face-painting and costume conventions.",
